   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to the commercial production credit",
    "basePrintNo": "S5998",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5998-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §28, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5998\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to the commercial production\ncredit\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nTo provide clarification for the the measuring standards applicable to\nthe growth credit and to amend the definition of production costs to\ninclude various techniques used in the industry.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nSection one of the bill makes two amendments to section 28 of the tax\nlaw.\n\nFirst, the bill clarifies the measuring standards to access the\n\"growth credit\" available to the qualified production companies as\npart of the empire state commercial production credit.\n\nSecond, the bill amends the definition of production costs so that\nvarious production techniques shall be deemed qualified production\ncosts.\n\nSection two of the bill provides the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThis technical amendment to the tax credit provides clarification of\nmeasuring standards and in the definition of qualified production\ncosts. The measuring standards are clarified to guide the calculation\nused by qualified production companies to access the \"growth credit\"\nas part of the empire state commercial production credit. The\ndefinition of qualified production costs is clarified to clearly\ninclude certain production techniques that are used in commercial\nproduction within the eligible qualified production costs.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
